    "summary": "Destination College Advising Corps is a college access program run by the Center for Educational Partnerships at the University of California, Berkeley. It places recent college graduates in high schools as full-time College Adviser Fellows. They help students with college applications, financial aid and campus visits. It serves schools in Alameda, Contra Costa and Santa Clara counties.",
